{
  // THE TEST FILES OF `@exodra/dom`, COMPILED — 53 suites, the largest set in the repository, and
  // the one that carried two of the three files the `exoStrPlan` → `strSchema` rename left red. The
  // scheme is written out once in `packages/core/tsconfig.tests.json`.
  //
  // `paths` IS RESTATED IN FULL because `extends` replaces it wholesale rather than merging. The
  // first four entries are the base's, unchanged; the last three are what the SUITES reach for and
  // the sources do not:
  //
  //   `@exodra/string`     — the renderer-divergence and conformance suites render the same schema
  //                          through both backends and compare. The live renderer itself never
  //                          imports the snapshot one, and `.dependency-cruiser.cjs` has a rule
  //                          saying so; this mapping is for test files only and adds no edge to
  //                          the crawl, which excludes `\.test\.`.
  //   `@exodra/test-utils` — `host()` / `detachedHost()` / `buildRow()` / `source()`, reached at
  //                          RUN time through the root `vitest.config.ts` alias. Nothing but that
  //                          alias has ever resolved this specifier, which is precisely why the
  //                          compiler needs to be told.
  //   `@exodra/dom`        — ITS OWN NAME, and leaving it out is what made this gate check the
  //                          wrong thing for as long as it has existed. 50 suites here import the
  //                          package by name rather than by relative path; with no mapping, node
  //                          resolution walks to `packages/dom/dist/index.d.ts` — a BUILD ARTEFACT,
  //                          and one `release:check` does not produce until `build:all`, six steps
  //                          AFTER this gate. So the suites were being typechecked against whatever
  //                          the last build happened to export, and agreement with the sources was
  //                          a coincidence that held only while the two agreed. It stopped holding
  //                          the moment the entry point changed: 67 errors, all of them
  //                          "`@exodra/dom` has no exported member `ExoDomBackend`", against a
  //                          barrel that exports it three times. Every other package in the repo
  //                          already maps `@exodra/dom` to `.tsbuild`; this is that line, for the
  //                          one package that needed it most and was the only one without it.
  //
  //                          IT POINTS AT `src/index.ts` AND NOT AT `.tsbuild`, which is the one
  //                          difference from every other entry above and the whole reason this
  //                          mapping works. The entries above name OTHER packages, which a
  //                          suite can only reach as built declarations. This one names THIS
  //                          package, whose sources these same suites also import by relative path
  //                          — `../dom/exo-dom-node` beside `@exodra/dom` in one file is
  //                          ordinary here. Point the specifier at `.tsbuild` and those two spell
  //                          DIFFERENT types with the same name: `TExoDomNode` from the build
  //                          and `TExoDomNode` from the source, structurally identical and
  //                          mutually unassignable because `TExoDomChild.mount` is typed `this`.
  //                          That produced 24 doppelganger errors whose message walked six levels
  //                          down to `plan` before naming the two paths. `src/index.ts` is the
  //                          identity the relative imports already have, so there is one type.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false,
    "incremental": false,
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@exodra/context": ["../context/.tsbuild/index.d.ts"],
      "@exodra/core": ["../core/.tsbuild/index.d.ts"],
      "@exodra/list-reconcile": ["../list-reconcile/.tsbuild/index.d.ts"],
      "@exodra/string": ["../string/.tsbuild/index.d.ts"],
      "@exodra/test-utils": ["../test-utils/.tsbuild/index.d.ts"],
      // The declarative machine half. Four suites here drive `withExoComputedMachine`,
      // `exoTransition` and `exoWiring` through this backend; the renderer itself names none of
      // them, which is why this is a test-only mapping and adds no edge to the crawl.
      "@exodra/computed": ["../computed/.tsbuild/index.d.ts"],
      "@exodra/dom": ["./src/index.ts"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["dist", ".tsbuild", "node_modules"]
}
